{"w":2400,"h":3406,"lines":[{"c":1,"y":0.04006043408622717,"w":0.064478607177734348,"h":0.015809363781250863,"x":0.89456482002188054,"t":"Test 3"},{"w":0.72371134440104168,"x":0.063917523582749186,"y":0.087199060479372648,"t":"JEREMY: No. But we need to write about the illustrations, because they're an essential","h":0.013211978860833917,"c":1},{"x":0.13814431956125287,"t":"element of children's experience of reading the stories. It's probably easiest for you","y":0.10305343500798914,"w":0.70309280395507812,"h":0.014679976512037562,"c":1},{"x":0.13603288977250852,"h":0.015519888066433563,"c":1,"t":"to write that section, as you know more about drawing than I do.","w":0.54649225870768225,"y":0.11879486617194845},{"t":"HELEN:","h":0.01026134860564587,"x":0.061839106048404202,"y":0.13803793017954702,"w":0.053641376495361326,"c":1},{"x":0.1360316317360529,"w":0.59805394490559893,"c":1,"t":"Maybe, but I find it quite hard to write about. I'd be happier if you did it.","h":0.016755026225405256,"y":0.13460223311322328},{"t":"JEREMY: OK. So when do you think ...","y":0.1500778432519656,"h":0.017913556280936827,"c":1,"x":0.059627218502004857,"w":0.32203653971354168},{"h":0.013081395479068947,"w":0.039175256093343158,"y":0.13372093012656294,"t":"Q30","c":1,"x":0.86391752649585418},{"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"w":0.16288659413655598,"t":"SECTION 4","x":0.06391752757089729,"y":0.2034644743943661},{"x":0.061855679163242125,"y":0.23253082798750868,"w":0.7587628682454427,"t":"So what l'm going to talk about to you today is something called Ethnography. This is a type","h":0.014679976512037562,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.06391752619417683,"t":"of research aimed at exploring the way human cultures work. It was first developed for use in","w":0.76907216389973965,"y":0.24854651156099417,"h":0.013081395479068947},{"t":"anthropology, and it's also been used in sociology and communication studies. So what's it","w":0.7525773111979166,"x":0.061855674217930999,"h":0.014679976512037562,"c":1,"y":0.26453317690057176},{"x":0.061791314914824889,"w":0.78153457641601554,"h":0.017984496658154936,"c":1,"y":0.27899167569088945,"t":"got to do with business, you may ask. Well, businesses are finding that ethnography can offer."},{"h":0.013081395479068947,"y":0.28052325571036296,"w":0.037113402684529562,"t":"Q31","x":0.86597938103493355,"c":1},{"w":0.77525772094726564,"t":"them deeper insight into the possible needs of customers, either present or future, as wel as","h":0.01453488361674482,"c":1,"y":0.29651162795496355,"x":0.059793819932913932},{"x":0.061798330940651167,"c":1,"w":0.7897900390625,"t":"providing valuable information about their attitudes towards existing products. And ethnography","h":0.017129131995854641,"y":0.31151556135330738},{"c":1,"x":0.061771737045356281,"h":0.01917130430516123,"t":"can also help companies to design new products or services that customers really want.","y":0.32618008630515927,"w":0.73002756754557285},{"w":0.77749720255533861,"h":0.018778304247315747,"c":1,"x":0.059719903816800868,"t":"Let's look at some examples of how ethnographic research works in business. One team of","y":0.35025421602533102},{"c":1,"h":0.014679976512037674,"t":"researchers did a project for a company manufacturing kitchen equipment. They watched","x":0.059793823515741827,"y":0.3690546097448596,"w":0.7587628682454427},{"x":0.061855677340998151,"y":0.38517441877179182,"h":0.015988371754420694,"w":0.76701029459635417,"c":1,"t":"how cooks used measuring cups to measure out things like sugar and flour. They saw that"},{"y":0.40105695821191145,"h":0.01614797416324143,"x":0.061855679291293292,"t":"the cooks had to check and recheck the contents, because although the measuring cups.","w":0.7587628682454427,"c":1},{"w":0.037113402684529562,"t":"Q32","x":0.86597938103493355,"y":0.40116279059408388,"c":1,"h":0.013081395479069058},{"h":0.014534883616744709,"t":"had numbers inside them. the cooks couldn'tsee these easily, So a new design of cup was","x":0.059793826644720223,"w":0.77319585164388016,"c":1,"y":0.41715116284056797},{"w":0.51141052246093754,"y":0.43303899814890412,"x":0.061819941095494407,"h":0.014553487265873022,"c":1,"t":"developed to overcome this problem, and it was a top seller."},{"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"t":"Another team of ethnographic researchers looked at how cell phones were used in Uganda,","y":0.45625366978937931,"w":0.78144327799479163,"x":0.059793827053357521},{"w":0.74442031860351565,"h":0.017394610733686422,"y":0.47233230808191706,"c":1,"t":"in Africa. They found that people who didn't have their own phones could pay to use the","x":0.059751351703251319},{"y":0.4882560187592957,"h":0.016147974163241319,"x":0.059793823929121949,"w":0.84329895019531254,"c":1,"t":"phones of local entrepreneurs. Because these customers paid in advance for their calls, they Q33"},{"x":0.059746170062469163,"t":"were eager to know how much time they'd spenton the call so far. So the phone company","y":0.50374555458419734,"w":0.76504145304361981,"c":1,"h":0.016627219307093544},{"c":1,"t":"designed phones for use globally with this added feature.","w":0.48659795125325522,"x":0.059793807790012983,"h":0.014679976512037562,"y":0.52172636544251605},{"t":"Ethnographic research has also been carried out in computer companies. In one company, IT","y":0.54492072816399206,"x":0.063917515707319877,"h":0.014679976512037674,"c":1,"w":0.78762888590494795},{"h":0.014534883616744709,"w":0.79175257364908858,"c":1,"x":0.059793816279630693,"t":"systems administrators were observed for several weeks. It was found that a large amount of","y":0.56104651167598463},{"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"t":"their work involved communicating with colleagues in order to solve problems, but that they","w":0.777319590250651,"x":0.059793813015854291,"y":0.5769230771943431},{"c":1,"h":0.013678104402874758,"w":0.039569740295410161,"t":"Q34","y":0.57673652915591667,"x":0.86372028438379511},{"t":"didn't have a standard way of exchanging information from spreadsheets and so on. So the.","w":0.78144327799479174,"y":0.59302325586218063,"x":0.059793824909711003,"h":0.01453488361674482,"c":1},{"h":0.014679976512037562,"y":0.60892542598805555,"w":0.60412368774414071,"t":"team came up with an idea for software that would help them to do this","c":1,"x":0.059793826216872459},{"c":1,"y":0.63226744202393137,"w":0.75051544189453123,"t":"In another piece of research, a team observed and talked to nurses working in hospitals.","x":0.059793825501677132,"h":0.016000320963207137},{"t":"This led to the recognition that the nurses needed to access the computer records of their","h":0.017062826151016286,"y":0.64764331837058831,"c":1,"x":0.059734151520950622,"w":0.76094340006510419},{"h":0.013081395479069058,"c":1,"w":0.039175256093343047,"x":0.86185567083143633,"y":0.64825581384989772,"t":"Q35"},{"t":"patients, no matter where they were. This led to the development of a portable computer","x":0.06185569264772596,"c":1,"h":0.016147974163241319,"y":0.66412213754332805,"w":0.74845357259114587},{"w":0.70515462239583337,"h":0.01453488361674482,"y":0.68168604656139864,"x":0.059793822727184628,"c":1,"t":"tablet that allowed the nurses to check records in locations throughout the hospital."},{"c":1,"y":0.70493247217099109,"t":"Occasionally, research can be done even in environments where the researchers can't be","h":0.014679976512037562,"w":0.75670104980468755,"x":0.063917516237216129},{"y":0.72078684669982074,"w":0.8391752624511718,"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"t":"present. For example, in one project done for an airline, respondents used their smartphones. Q36","x":0.061855667650397003},{"w":0.7216494750976562,"c":1,"h":0.01453488361674482,"t":"to record information during airline trips, in a study aiming at tracking the emotions of","x":0.059793812502718376,"y":0.73691860452156943},{"w":0.22300392150878906,"h":0.015944633775085038,"x":0.061712814589640175,"y":0.7530369100375327,"t":"passengers during a flight.","c":1},{"h":0.015988371754420583,"w":0.76288660685221354,"x":0.059793809906117969,"y":0.8008720931861103,"c":1,"t":"So what makes studies like these different from ordinary research? Let's look at some of the"},{"x":0.059793806599270451,"t":"general principles behind ethnographic research in business. First of all, the researcher has to","w":0.77938145955403648,"y":0.81679389286234505,"h":0.01614797416324143,"c":1},{"t":"be completely open-minded - he or she hasn't thought up a hypothesis to be tested, as is the","w":0.77319585164388016,"h":0.015988371754420694,"c":1,"x":0.059793828961565036,"y":0.83284883721872005},{"h":0.016147974163241319,"c":1,"x":0.059793826696774771,"t":"case in other types of research. Instead they wait for the participants in the research to inform","y":0.84879624179246405,"w":0.77319585164388016},{"h":0.015988371754420583,"t":"them. As far as choosing the participants themselves is concemed, that's not really all that","y":0.86482558155490108,"c":1,"w":0.74845362345377608,"x":0.059793807029712411},{"w":0.7587628682454427,"x":0.059793823500781398,"c":1,"h":0.014679976512037562,"t":"different from ordinary research - the criteria according to which the participants are chosen","y":0.88226658847554362},{"t":"may be something as simple as the age bracket they fall into, or the researchers may select","y":0.89476924121948453,"x":0.059659485969095462,"h":0.021576133813146825,"w":0.76317545572916667,"c":1},{"y":0.91424418621326697,"w":0.78144327799479163,"c":1,"x":0.06185568049469168,"t":"them according to their income, or they might try to find a set of people who all use a particular","h":0.015988371754420694},{"y":0.95282612250927956,"w":0.29151685078938799,"c":1,"x":0.35218486537986032,"h":0.022673451753483009,"t":"leltsresources.org"},{"y":0.89457443587027197,"w":0.042288262049357095,"h":0.017656311734032148,"c":1,"x":0.86246242503887216,"t":"Q37"},{"w":0.039175256093343158,"h":0.013081395479069058,"x":0.91340206257188505,"y":0.94476744175687455,"c":1,"t":"117"}]}